#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""arenactl: Argus Arena's one command, from a checkout of its repository.

    ./arenactl doctor [--for TASK]       what this machine has for a task, and how to get the rest
    ./arenactl install [options]         install from this checkout: builds the images, then the installer
    ./arenactl upgrade|repair [options]  the same for an installation there already
    ./arenactl status|remove|verify|features|requirements [options]   the installer's own commands
    ./arenactl build [--with A,B] [--without A,B] [--all]   the stack's images (built and pulled)
    ./arenactl code-arena [RID ...] [--offline]             Code Arena's packages for each system, in dist/
    ./arenactl deps [--arch amd64|arm64]                    Docker, Compose and NVIDIA's toolkit, for a bundle
    ./arenactl bundle [--with-deps] [--models] [--packs]    the offline installer: dist/argus-arena-VERSION-offline.run
    ./arenactl cert|sign|backup|restore|hosts|kube [args]   the operator's scripts, for an installation
    ./arenactl check NAME [args]          the live checks (functional, compliance, recovery, gpu, ...)
    ./arenactl test [SUITE ...]           the test suites (app, code-arena, argus, web, deploy)
    ./arenactl scripts                    every script in the repository, by what it is for

Python 3.8 or newer and nothing else to install for itself: on Windows, `python arenactl ...`.
Building and packaging work on Linux, macOS and Windows; installing runs on Linux (the stack is
Linux containers). docs/scripts.md says more, with every option.
"""
